# RS_HandHUD bracer -- the plate as a TRIPTYCH so it sits on a wrist instead
# of hovering over one.
#
# Same footprint as rs_plate.obj: X is the LONG axis (along the forearm) and
# runs -1..1, Y goes across the wrist and runs -1..1, +Z faces the reader.
# MODELDEF Scale turns those into map units, so this is a drop-in swap for the
# flat quad and the placement tuned for that quad still reads.
#
# THE FOLD IS ABOUT THE LONG AXIS. Split into three strips across Y and hinge
# the outer two back 40 degrees, so the middle panel faces you square and the
# two flanking it follow the wrist down its sides. A flat slab this wide either
# floats off the arm at its edges or buries them in it; this does neither.
#
#   hinges at y = +/-1/3, outer edge lands at y = +/-0.8440, z = -0.4285
#   (1/3 + 2/3*cos40, -2/3*sin40)
#
# UVs ARE CONTINUOUS ACROSS ALL THREE PANELS: v runs 0..1 over the whole
# shape exactly as it did over the flat quad, so the canvas is one image
# wrapped over a fold rather than three images that have to be authored
# separately. Content can be split per panel later by choosing where the rows
# land in the canvas; the geometry does not care.
#
# Text upside down or mirrored? That is the canvas' own bottom-up sampling,
# not this file -- see fy() in rs_handhud.zs. Swap the vt column here only if
# the FLAT plate was right and this one is not.

# bottom folded edge
v -1.00000 -0.84400 -0.42850
v  1.00000 -0.84400 -0.42850
# bottom hinge
v -1.00000 -0.33333  0.00000
v  1.00000 -0.33333  0.00000
# top hinge
v -1.00000  0.33333  0.00000
v  1.00000  0.33333  0.00000
# top folded edge
v -1.00000  0.84400 -0.42850
v  1.00000  0.84400 -0.42850

vt 0.0 0.00000
vt 1.0 0.00000
vt 0.0 0.33333
vt 1.0 0.33333
vt 0.0 0.66667
vt 1.0 0.66667
vt 0.0 1.00000
vt 1.0 1.00000

# one normal per panel, and the same three flipped for the back faces
vn  0.00000 -0.64279  0.76604
vn  0.00000  0.00000  1.00000
vn  0.00000  0.64279  0.76604
vn  0.00000  0.64279 -0.76604
vn  0.00000  0.00000 -1.00000
vn  0.00000 -0.64279 -0.76604

# ---- front -----------------------------------------------------------------
# lower panel
f 1/1/1 2/2/1 4/4/1
f 1/1/1 4/4/1 3/3/1
# centre panel
f 3/3/2 4/4/2 6/6/2
f 3/3/2 6/6/2 5/5/2
# upper panel
f 5/5/3 6/6/3 8/8/3
f 5/5/3 8/8/3 7/7/3

# ---- back, same UVs so it is never invisible from behind -------------------
f 1/1/6 4/4/6 2/2/6
f 1/1/6 3/3/6 4/4/6
f 3/3/5 6/6/5 4/4/5
f 3/3/5 5/5/5 6/6/5
f 5/5/4 8/8/4 6/6/4
f 5/5/4 7/7/4 8/8/4
